      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How should warehouse operators size a robot fleet?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Robot fleet size is determined by peak demand divided by robot productivity rate. Fleet size must also be evaluated against average annual demand to assess utilization. Compare peak and average demand using the same task units and time basis. A larger gap may create idle capacity; no numeric peak-to-average cutoff establishes investment viability."
